ENFORCEMENT DECREE OF THE ACT ON INTEGRATED SUPPORT FOR COMMUNITY CARE INCLUDING MEDICAL CARE AND LONG-TERM CARE

Article 1 (Purpose)
The purpose of this Decree is to prescribe matters delegated by the Act on Integrated Support for Community Care Including Medical Care and Long-Term Care and matters necessary for its enforcement.

Article 2 (Persons Eligible for Integrated Support)
(1) "Persons prescribed by Presidential Decree" in subparagraph 2 of Article 2 of the Act on Integrated Support for Community Care Including Medical Care and Long-Term Care (hereinafter referred to as the "Act") means persons falling under any of the following subparagraphs who have difficulty maintaining their daily lives due to frailty, disability, illness, an accident, or similar circumstances (hereinafter referred to as "frailty, etc.") and require support addressing multiple needs:
1. A person aged 65 or older;
2. A person with a disability registered as a person with a severe degree of disability pursuant to Article 32 of the Act on Welfare of Persons with Disabilities, whom the Minister of Health and Welfare recognizes as needing integrated support;
3. Other persons belonging to vulnerable groups, etc. in need of integrated support, recognized in consultation with the Minister of Health and Welfare by a Special Metropolitan City Mayor, Metropolitan City Mayor, Special Self-Governing City Mayor, Do Governor, Special Self-Governing Province Governor, or the head of a Si (including an administrative mayor under Article 11 (1) of the Special Act on the Establishment of Jeju Special Self-Governing Province and the Development of Free International City; hereinafter the same shall apply), Gun, or Gu (meaning the head of an autonomous Gu; hereinafter referred to as the "head of a Si/Gun/Gu").
(2) The Minister of Health and Welfare shall determine detailed criteria, priorities, and other matters for cases in which a person falling under paragraph (1) 1 or 2 has difficulty maintaining daily life due to frailty, etc. and requires support addressing multiple needs.

Article 3 (Changes to Important Matters in Master Plan)
"Important matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the latter part of Article 5 (4) of the Act means the following matters:
1. Matters falling under Article 5 (2) 1, 4, and 5 of the Act;
2. Matters related to the affairs of two or more central administrative agencies or Special Metropolitan Cities, Metropolitan Cities, Special Self-Governing Cities, Dos, or Special Self-Governing Provinces.

Article 4 (Cases Requiring Ex Officio Applications)
"Persons in need of urgent support prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the former part of Article 10 (2) of the Act means persons falling under any of the following subparagraphs who have difficulty applying for integrated support pursuant to Article 10 (1) of the Act:
1. A person whose application for long-term care benefits under the Act on Long-Term Care Insurance for Senior Citizens has been denied;
2. A person whose application for activity support benefits under the Act on Activity Assistance for Persons with Disabilities has been denied;
3. A person who has just been discharged from a medical institution under Article 3 of the Medical Service Act;
4. A person in a crisis situation under Article 2 of the Emergency Aid and Support Act who has difficulty waiting for other support;
5. A person who needs emergency care services due to the occurrence of a disaster, etc. under Article 10 (1) 1 of the Act on Support for Social Services and Establishment and Operation of Public Agencies for Social Service and has difficulty waiting for other support;
6. A person who is unable to live independently on their own and for whom care by family members or other guardians is substantially difficult.

Article 5 (Comprehensive Assessment)
(1) Where the head of a Si/Gun/Gu receives an application for integrated support or identifies a person eligible for integrated support pursuant to Article 10 (1) and (2) of the Act, the head shall comprehensively assess, pursuant to Article 12 (1) of the Act, the need for medical support and the need for long-term care and other care in daily life, etc. that are necessary to enable the person eligible for integrated support to continue living a healthy life in the place where the person has been living, taking into account the following matters:
1. Physical functions and ability to perform activities of daily living as affected by frailty, etc.;
2. The need for medical services, including whether the person has an illness;
3. Nutritional status;
4. Residential environment;
5. Other matters that the Minister of Health and Welfare deems necessary for determining the need for medical support and the need for long-term care and other care in daily life, etc.
(2) Pursuant to Article 12 (3) of the Act, the head of a Si/Gun/Gu shall entrust part of the investigation work necessary for the comprehensive assessment under paragraph (1) to a specialized institution designated by the Minister of Health and Welfare pursuant to Article 25 of the Act (hereinafter referred to as a "specialized institution").
(3) Matters necessary for comprehensive assessment under Article 12 of the Act, other than those prescribed in paragraphs (1) and (2), shall be determined by the Minister of Health and Welfare.

Article 6 (Establishment and Operation of Integrated Support Information System)
(1) "Data prescribed by Presidential Decree, such as data on the housing and income of persons eligible for integrated support" in the former part of Article 22 (2) of the Act means the following data:
1. Where home-based health and medical support is needed among the health and medical services under Article 15 of the Act, data on health and other matters for such support;
2. Data on the current receipt and history of receipt of social security benefits under the Framework Act on Social Security, etc.;
3. Data on the use of social welfare facilities under the Social Welfare Services Act;
4. Computer networks or data under Article 3 (2) of the Enforcement Decree of the Act on the Use and Provision of Social Security Benefits and Search for Eligible Beneficiaries;
5. Data on the types of disabilities under Article 2 of the Enforcement Decree of the Act on Welfare of Persons with Disabilities;
6. Other data that the Minister of Health and Welfare deems necessary for handling integrated support affairs and publicly notifies.
(2) "Information systems prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 22 (3) 6 of the Act means the following systems:
1. The information system for computerizing the affairs of social welfare facilities under Article 6-2 (1) of the Social Welfare Services Act;
2. The integrated support system for public agencies for social service under Article 38 (1) of the Act on Support for Social Services and Establishment and Operation of Public Agencies for Social Service;
3. The system related to health and health care information on persons with disabilities under Article 12 (2) of the Act on Guarantee of Right to Health and Access to Medical Services for Persons with Disabilities;
4. The comprehensive hospice information system under Article 28-2 (1) of the Act on Hospice and Palliative Care and Decisions on Life-Sustaining Treatment for Patients at the End of Life;
5. The computer system under Article 20-3 (4) of the Enforcement Decree of the Act on Welfare of Persons with Disabilities;
6. Other information systems that the Minister of Health and Welfare recognizes as requiring linkage with the integrated support information system under Article 22 (1) of the Act for integrated support affairs.

Article 7 (Provision and Use of Information)
"Information prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 23 (2) of the Act means the following information:
1. Information included in the content of fact-finding surveys under Article 7 of the Act;
2. Where a plan for support in health and medical care, etc. for a person eligible for integrated support, formulated under other statutes or regulations as referred to in the proviso of Article 13 (1) of the Act, has been prepared comprehensively, its content;
3. The content of investigation work entrusted to and performed by a specialized institution pursuant to Article 5 (2);
4. The status of applications for benefits administered by specialized institutions under other statutes or regulations, the status and history of receipt of such benefits (including the grade where there are grades), and, where an application for benefits has been dismissed on procedural grounds or denied on the merits, the grounds for the dismissal or denial.

Article 8 (Entrustment of Functions)
(1) The Minister of Health and Welfare and the heads of local governments may entrust part of the functions referred to in Article 29 (2) 1 through 3 of the Act to a person falling under any of the following subparagraphs:
1. A specialized institution;
2. An institution related to integrated support;
3. Other institutions or organizations that the Minister of Health and Welfare recognizes as having expertise in integrated support affairs.
(2) Where the Minister of Health and Welfare or the head of a local government entrusts functions pursuant to paragraph (1), the Minister or the head shall publish the entrusted institution, the details of the entrusted functions, and other relevant matters in the Official Gazette, an official bulletin, or on a website.

Article 9 (Processing of Sensitive Information and Personally Identifiable Information)
(1) Where unavoidable for performing any of the following affairs, the Minister of Health and Welfare (including persons entrusted with the functions of the Minister of Health and Welfare pursuant to Articles 22 (4) and 29 (2) of the Act) may process information concerning health under Article 23 of the Personal Information Protection Act and data containing resident registration numbers or alien registration numbers under subparagraph 1 or 4 of Article 19 of the Enforcement Decree of that Act:
1. Affairs concerning fact-finding surveys under Article 7 of the Act;
2. Affairs concerning evaluation of the implementation performance of regional plans under Article 9 of the Act;
3. Affairs concerning the establishment and operation of the integrated support information system under Article 22 of the Act.
(2) Where unavoidable for performing any of the following affairs, the head of a Si/Gun/Gu (including a person to whom the relevant authority has been delegated or entrusted, where such authority has been delegated or entrusted) may process information concerning health under Article 23 of the Personal Information Protection Act and data containing resident registration numbers or alien registration numbers under subparagraph 1 or 4 of Article 19 of the Enforcement Decree of that Act:
1. Affairs concerning applications for integrated support, identification of eligible persons, investigations, etc. under Article 10 of the Act;
2. Affairs concerning referral and linkage of discharged patients, etc. under Article 11 of the Act;
3. Affairs concerning comprehensive assessment under Article 12 of the Act;
4. Affairs concerning formulation of individual support plans under Article 13 of the Act;
5. Affairs concerning provision of and requests for integrated support and regular checks on the status of integrated support provision and changes in the condition of eligible persons under Article 14 (1) and (4) of the Act;
6. Affairs concerning provision and use of information under Article 23 (1) and (3) of the Act.
(3) Where unavoidable for performing any of the following affairs, a specialized institution may process information concerning health under Article 23 of the Personal Information Protection Act and data containing resident registration numbers or alien registration numbers under subparagraph 1 or 4 of Article 19 of the Enforcement Decree of that Act:
1. Affairs concerning provision and use of information under Article 23 (2) and (3) of the Act;
2. Affairs concerning the functions referred to in the subparagraphs of Article 25 (1) of the Act.
(4) Where unavoidable for performing any of the following affairs, an institution related to integrated support may process information concerning health under Article 23 of the Personal Information Protection Act and data containing resident registration numbers or alien registration numbers under subparagraph 1 or 4 of Article 19 of the Enforcement Decree of that Act:
1. Affairs concerning provision of integrated support under Article 14 (3) of the Act;
2. Affairs concerning provision and use of information under Article 23 (2) and (3) of the Act.

ADDENDA <Presidential Decree No. 35897, Dec. 9, 2025>

Article 1 (Enforcement Date)
This Decree shall enter into force on March 27, 2026.

Article 2 (Transitional Measures concerning Persons Covered by Pilot Projects for Integrated Support)
A person who, as at the time this Decree enters into force, has been selected as a person covered by a pilot project under Article 26 of the Act and is receiving integrated support services shall be deemed a person eligible for integrated support under this Decree.
